{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794045777,"nonce":"udIWwXkBkbISiCY+cpIiXPqqr3Y=","message":"**hl.Bytes at the extern boundary: what rayzor.Bytes gives**\n\nRead from rayzor/compiler/haxe-std; nothing run.\n\n- On Rayzor `haxe.io.Bytes` is a typedef of `rayzor.Bytes`, an extern class over the runtime's native byte vector (pointer, length, capacity). The plugin ABI reads it through rayzor_plugin_bytes_data/len/new, and strings through rayzor_plugin_string_data/len/new. rayzor-gpu already takes `haxe.io.Bytes` for writeBuffer/writeTexture, as hlwgpu does.\n- So the portable boundary type is `haxe.io.Bytes` for buffers and `String` for text. On HashLink the inline externs unwrap it (`bytes.getData()` is the hl.Bytes) at no cost; on Rayzor it passes through. This is cleaner than a custom abstract.\n\n**What ashui uses and the match**\n\nOutside the externs, hl.Bytes appears in about 19 files: carets and clip-path scratch buffers (TextEditing, TextField, ClipPath), the display-list byte compare (Renderer), Utf8, menu JSON, canvaskit. Operations used, with counts: getF32 39, getI32 14, setF32 8, setI32 4, setUI8 2, blit 5, compare 6, sub 40, alloc 23, copy 23, fromUTF8 8.\n\n- getF32/setF32 -\u003e getFloat/setFloat. getI32/setI32 -\u003e getInt32/setInt32. setUI8 -\u003e set. blit -\u003e blit(pos, src, srcPos, len). alloc -\u003e alloc. All little-endian, matching.\n- Gap: `compare(pos, other, otherPos, len)` is ranged on hl.Bytes; rayzor.Bytes.compare takes only another buffer. The Renderer's display-list diff (6 uses on the hot path) needs a ranged compare helper, probably in the runtime, not a Haxe loop.\n- Gap: Utf8.encode/decode exist because HashLink strings are UTF-16 and the native library wants NUL-terminated UTF-8. On Rayzor the plugin takes Strings directly, so these become pass-through.\n- Check: sub() on rayzor.Bytes is documented as a view sharing the owner's data; under ownership a view must not outlive its owner. ashui's 40 sub() calls and the 23 copy() calls need checking against that.\n- Check: out-parameter buffers (carets, info) are written by the native side through the buffer's data pointer; that fits the ABI but needs a test.\n- Not in rayzor.Bytes: getUI16/setUI16, getF64-style helpers beyond getDouble/setDouble. ashui does not use them.\n\n**Next step**\n\nPhase 3 of this issue: change the extern signatures to haxe.io.Bytes/String on all branches, with the HashLink wrappers inline, then ask the Rayzor runtime owner for a ranged compare.","files":null}]}